karr sync silently reports success on failure, and cannot sync to ProxyCommand-only remotes. Two distinct issues found while syncing a board to a remote that is defined solely by an ssh-config Host alias (HostName + ProxyCommand jump host), where the real IP has no direct route.

--- Bug A (high): Cmd/Sync.pm swallows pull/push failures ---
In App::karr::Cmd::Sync::execute the return values of $git->pull and $git->push are ignored:

    $git->pull;      # return value discarded
    ...
    $git->push;      # return value discarded
    say "Done.";     # printed unconditionally

App::karr::Git::pull/push catch the libgit2 exception in try/catch, stash it in _last_error, and return 0. Sync never checks, so "Done." is printed even when nothing was transferred. Result: the operator believes the board synced when it did not -- silent divergence between local and remote refs/karr.

By contrast Role::SyncLifecycle::sync_before/sync_after (used by move/edit/create) DO check the return value and croak, so those commands correctly surface the failure. Only `karr sync` hides it.

Fix: check the boolean from pull/push, print $git->last_error on failure, and exit non-zero. "Done." only when both legs actually succeeded.

--- Bug B (design): all-libgit2 transport cannot use ssh-config aliases / ProxyCommand ---
App::karr::Git does every remote op via Git::Native/libgit2 ("all-native ... no fork/exec"). libgit2/libssh2 does not read ~/.ssh/config and cannot execute a ProxyCommand. A remote whose reachability depends on an ssh-config Host alias (alias -> HostName + ProxyCommand) is therefore unreachable from ANY karr path, deterministically:

    App::karr::Git->new(dir=>'.')->pull
    => libgit2 error -1 (klass 12): failed to resolve address for <alias>: No address associated with hostname

The same remote works flawlessly via the git CLI (`git push origin '+refs/karr/*:refs/karr/*'`), because the CLI applies the ssh-config ProxyCommand. This is not a libgit2 bug (ssh-config is an OpenSSH feature libgit2 deliberately omits) -- it is karr's choice of libgit2-only with no CLI fallback.

Fix direction: either (a) add a git-CLI fallback transport for sync when libgit2 cannot connect, or (b) document that the configured remote must be a libgit2-resolvable URL (no ssh-config aliases / ProxyCommand). At minimum, Bug A must be fixed so this failure is never silent.

Repro remote shape: Host alias with `HostName <ip>` + `ProxyCommand ssh <jump> ...`, real IP not directly routable. `karr sync --pull` prints "Done." (Bug A) while `karr move` correctly fails resolution (Bug B).
